# Security (public repository)

This repo is public. Treat every commit as world-readable.

## Never commit

`.env`, API keys, `TYTO_HOST_TOKEN`, browser `tmp/` profiles, cookies,
`Set-Cookie` / `Authorization` values, vault ciphertext, private keys.

Copy `.env.example` → `.env` locally. If a live secret is committed: **rotate**,
do not only delete the file.

Scanners (must stay green): `npm run secrets:scan`, gitleaks, GitHub secret scanning.

Do not print secret values in logs, test output, or chat.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
console.log("cookie", hdr);

// ✅ GOOD
tape.push("network", redactor.safe(hdr));
```

## Identity

Auth material is **data AND secret**. Encrypted at rest; DEK in OS keychain
(memory fake in tests). Restore **only** into the browser. No OS ticket harvest,
no impersonation.

Cookie/token values leave the host only to the **power** scope (the `tyto`
CLI) when the request says `reveal: true`. Masked otherwise. Never persisted
raw, never sent to `ModelPort`, never to the safe scope (Perch, MCP).

Capture/restore requires an explicit origin grant. Expired bundles yield to
the operator — do not replay a dead session.

## Control plane

Host and debug port: `127.0.0.1` + token. Reject non-loopback `Host` and
foreign `Origin`. Never serve a token to an unauthenticated request.
Extension (deferred): native messaging only; no `window.tyto`. The agent
confirms submit / purchase / delete / send.
